# Unit 25 单词



## surrender
- **音标**: /səˈrendər/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 投降；放弃
- **例句**: The army was forced to surrender after a long siege.
- **近义词**: give up, yield, capitulate
- **派生词**: surrendering (n.)

## survive
- **音标**: /sərˈvaɪv/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 幸存；存活
- **例句**: Only a few people survived the earthquake.
- **近义词**: endure, live through, last
- **派生词**: survival (n.), survivor (n.), surviving (adj.)

## suspect
- **音标**: /səˈspekt/
- **词性**: v. n. adj.
- **释义**: 怀疑；嫌疑犯
- **例句**: The police suspect him of theft.
- **近义词**: doubt, distrust, believe
- **派生词**: suspicion (n.), suspicious (adj.), suspiciously (adv.)

## suspend
- **音标**: /səˈspend/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 暂停；悬挂；悬浮
- **例句**: The company suspended operations during the pandemic.
- **近义词**: pause, halt, hang
- **派生词**: suspension (n.), suspended (adj.)

## sustain
- **音标**: /səˈsteɪn/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 维持；承受；遭受
- **例句**: The economy cannot sustain such rapid growth.
- **近义词**: maintain, support, endure
- **派生词**: sustainable (adj.), sustainability (n.), sustained (adj.)

## swallow
- **音标**: /ˈswɑːloʊ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 吞咽；忍受
- **例句**: He swallowed the medicine with a glass of water.
- **近义词**: gulp, consume, accept
- **派生词**: swallowing (n.)

## swap
- **音标**: /swɑːp/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 交换；替换
- **例句**: They swapped seats during the meeting.
- **近义词**: exchange, trade, switch
- **派生词**: swappable (adj.)

## sweep
- **音标**: /swiːp/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 扫除；席卷；范围
- **例句**: The storm swept across the region.
- **近义词**: clean, brush, spread
- **派生词**: sweeping (adj.)

## swift
- **音标**: /swɪft/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 迅速的；敏捷的
- **例句**: The government took swift action to address the crisis.
- **近义词**: fast, quick, rapid
- **派生词**: swiftly (adv.), swiftness (n.)

## swing
- **音标**: /swɪŋ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 摇摆；摆动；秋千
- **例句**: The pendulum swings back and forth.
- **近义词**: sway, wave, oscillate
- **派生词**: swinging (adj.)

## switch
- **音标**: /swɪtʃ/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 转换；开关
- **例句**: She switched from medicine to law.
- **近义词**: change, shift, swap
- **派生词**: switching (n.)

## symbol
- **音标**: /ˈsɪmbl/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 象征；符号
- **例句**: The dove is a symbol of peace.
- **近义词**: sign, emblem, representation
- **派生词**: symbolic (adj.), symbolically (adv.), symbolize (v.)

## sympathize
- **音标**: /ˈsɪmpəθaɪz/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 同情；赞同
- **例句**: I sympathize with your situation.
- **近义词**: empathize, understand, support
- **派生词**: sympathy (n.), sympathetic (adj.), sympathetically (adv.)

## symptom
- **音标**: /ˈsɪmptəm/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 症状；征兆
- **例句**: Fever is a common symptom of the flu.
- **近义词**: sign, indication, manifestation
- **派生词**: symptomatic (adj.)

## tackle
- **音标**: /ˈtækl/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 处理；解决；阻截
- **例句**: The government needs to tackle the problem of poverty.
- **近义词**: deal with, address, handle
- **派生词**: tackling (n.)

## target
- **音标**: /ˈtɑːrɡɪt/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 目标；靶子；针对
- **例句**: The campaign targets young voters.
- **近义词**: goal, aim, objective
- **派生词**: targeted (adj.)

## task
- **音标**: /tæsk/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 任务；工作
- **例句**: The task of rebuilding the city will take years.
- **近义词**: job, assignment, duty

## tax
- **音标**: /tæks/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 税；征税
- **例句**: The government raised taxes on luxury goods.
- **近义词**: levy, duty, tariff
- **派生词**: taxation (n.), taxpayer (n.), taxable (adj.)

## tear
- **音标**: /ter/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 撕裂；眼泪
- **例句**: She tore the letter into pieces.
- **近义词**: rip, split, pull apart
- **派生词**: tearing (adj.), tearful (adj.)

## technique
- **音标**: /tekˈniːk/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 技术；技巧
- **例句**: The artist used a unique technique in this painting.
- **近义词**: method, skill, approach
- **派生词**: technical (adj.), technically (adv.), technician (n.)

## technology
- **音标**: /tekˈnɑːlədʒi/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 技术；科技
- **例句**: Technology has changed the way we live.
- **近义词**: tech, innovation, engineering
- **派生词**: technological (adj.), technologically (adv.), technologist (n.)

## temporary
- **音标**: /ˈtempəreri/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 临时的；暂时的
- **例句**: The company hired temporary workers for the busy season.
- **近义词**: short-term, provisional, interim
- **派生词**: temporarily (adv.), permanent (反义)

## tend
- **音标**: /tend/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 倾向于；照料
- **例句**: People tend to eat more during winter.
- **近义词**: incline, lean, be apt to
- **派生词**: tendency (n.), tender (adj.), tendency (n.)

## tense
- **音标**: /tens/
- **词性**: adj. n.
- **释义**: 紧张的；时态
- **例句**: The atmosphere in the room was tense.
- **近义词**: nervous, strained, anxious
- **派生词**: tension (n.), tensely (adv.)

## terminal
- **音标**: /ˈtɜːrmɪnl/
- **词性**: n. adj.
- **释义**: 终端；航站楼；晚期的
- **例句**: The new airport terminal opened last year.
- **近义词**: station, end, final
- **派生词**: terminate (v.), termination (n.)

## theme
- **音标**: /θiːm/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 主题；题目
- **例句**: The theme of the conference is innovation.
- **近义词**: topic, subject, motif
- **派生词**: thematic (adj.), thematically (adv.)

## theory
- **音标**: /ˈθiːəri/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 理论；学说
- **例句**: Einstein's theory of relativity changed physics.
- **近义词**: hypothesis, concept, principle
- **派生词**: theoretical (adj.), theoretically (adv.), theorist (n.)

## therapy
- **音标**: /ˈθerəpi/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 治疗；疗法
- **例句**: Physical therapy helped him recover from the injury.
- **近义词**: treatment, cure, remedy
- **派生词**: therapeutic (adj.), therapist (n.)

## thorough
- **音标**: /ˈθɜːroʊ/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 彻底的；仔细的
- **例句**: The police conducted a thorough investigation.
- **近义词**: complete, comprehensive, detailed
- **派生词**: thoroughly (adv.), thoroughness (n.)

## threat
- **音标**: /θret/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 威胁；恐吓
- **例句**: Climate change is a threat to the environment.
- **近义词**: danger, risk, menace
- **派生词**: threaten (v.), threatening (adj.), threateningly (adv.)

## thrive
- **音标**: /θraɪv/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 繁荣；兴旺
- **例句**: The business has thrived under her leadership.
- **近义词**: flourish, prosper, succeed
- **派生词**: thriving (adj.)

## tide
- **音标**: /taɪd/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 潮汐；潮流；趋势
- **例句**: The tide of public opinion is turning.
- **近义词**: current, trend, flow
- **派生词**: tidal (adj.)

## tighten
- **音标**: /ˈtaɪtn/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 加紧；变紧
- **例句**: The government tightened security after the incident.
- **近义词**: strengthen, constrict, firm up
- **派生词**: tight (adj.), tightly (adv.), tightness (n.)

## tolerance
- **音标**: /ˈtɑːlərəns/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 容忍；宽容；耐受性
- **例句**: We should show tolerance towards people of different cultures.
- **近义词**: patience, acceptance, endurance
- **派生词**: tolerate (v.), tolerant (adj.), intolerant (adj.)

## tone
- **音标**: /toʊn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 语气；音调；色调
- **例句**: I don't like the tone of his voice.
- **近义词**: sound, mood, shade
- **派生词**: tonal (adj.), toneless (adj.)

## torture
- **音标**: /ˈtɔːrtʃər/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 折磨；拷问
- **例句**: The prisoners were subjected to torture.
- **近义词**: torment, abuse, suffering
- **派生词**: torturous (adj.)

## tough
- **音标**: /tʌf/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 坚韧的；困难的；强硬的
- **例句**: It was a tough decision to make.
- **近义词**: difficult, hard, strong
- **派生词**: toughly (adv.), toughness (n.), toughen (v.)

## trace
- **音标**: /treɪs/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 追踪；痕迹；微量
- **例句**: The police traced the call to a payphone.
- **近义词**: track, follow, trail
- **派生词**: traceable (adj.), traceability (n.)

## tradition
- **音标**: /trəˈdɪʃn/
- **词性**: n.
- **释义**: 传统；惯例
- **例句**: It is a tradition to eat turkey on Thanksgiving.
- **近义词**: custom, convention, heritage
- **派生词**: traditional (adj.), traditionally (adv.), traditionalist (n.)

## trail
- **音标**: /treɪl/
- **词性**: n. v.
- **释义**: 小径；痕迹；追踪
- **例句**: We followed the trail through the forest.
- **近义词**: path, track, route
- **派生词**: trailer (n.), trailing (adj.)

## transfer
- **音标**: /trænsˈfɜːr/
- **词性**: v. n.
- **释义**: 转移；转让；调动
- **例句**: He transferred to a different department.
- **近义词**: move, shift, convey
- **派生词**: transferable (adj.), transference (n.)

## transform
- **音标**: /trænsˈfɔːrm/
- **词性**: v.
- **释义**: 转变；改造
- **例句**: Technology has transformed the way we communicate.
- **近义词**: change, convert, alter
- **派生词**: transformation (n.), transformative (adj.)

## transparent
- **音标**: /trænsˈpærənt/
- **词性**: adj.
- **释义**: 透明的；明显的
- **例句**: The company should be more transparent about its finances.
- **近义词**: clear, see-through, obvious
- **派生词**: transparency (n.), transparently (adv.)
